## Equipment

### Patrol Vests

Deputies may wear an external Sheriff patrol vest as part of the Class B or Class C uniform. Vest wear is **optional** and at the deputy's discretion.

Where a vest is worn, it must:

- Be department-issued or department-approved in appearance
- Display SBCSD identification, the deputy's name, and rank insignia
- Carry duty equipment in a professional, consistent layout

### Radio Requirement

**Every deputy must be able to communicate at all times.**

<Warning>
  A deputy who is not wearing a patrol vest **must** have a radio visibly carried on the uniform. There is no configuration in which a deputy is on duty without a radio.
</Warning>

| Configuration | Radio Requirement |
| --- | --- |
| Patrol vest worn | Radio carried on the vest |
| No patrol vest | Radio worn on the uniform or duty belt, visible |

The vest is optional. The radio is not.

### Body-Worn Cameras

Every deputy must have a body-worn camera equipped before going 10-8. This applies to all three uniform classes and is not waived by rank or assignment.

