## Grooming Standards

### Facial Hair

Beards are permitted. Deputies who choose to wear a beard must keep it:

- Neatly trimmed and maintained
- Clean and groomed at the start of every shift
- Free of styling that would interfere with professional appearance

Mustaches, goatees, and clean-shaven are equally acceptable. The standard is maintenance, not style — an unkempt beard is a uniform violation in the same way an untucked shirt is.

### Hair

Hair is kept clean and neat. Where hair length would interfere with the proper wear of a duty cover or equipment, it is secured.

### Tattoos

<AccordionGroup>
  <Accordion title="Permitted" icon="check">
    - **Arms** — full sleeve tattoos are permitted, on both upper and lower arms
    - **Hands** — hand and finger tattoos are permitted
    - **Neck** — permitted where not obscene or extremist in content
    - **Torso and legs** — permitted (not visible in uniform)
  </Accordion>

  <Accordion title="Prohibited" icon="x">
    - **Face** — no facial tattoos of any kind. This includes forehead, cheeks, nose, chin, and around the eyes.
    - **Any location** — tattoos depicting extremist symbols, hate speech, gang affiliation, obscene imagery, or content that would discredit the department
  </Accordion>
</AccordionGroup>

No deputy is required to cover a permitted tattoo. Sleeve length is a comfort choice, not a concealment requirement.

<Note>
  A tattoo that falls under the prohibited content rules is a conduct matter regardless of placement, including on areas normally covered by the uniform.
</Note>

### Jewelry and Accessories

Kept minimal and professional. Nothing that presents a safety hazard during a physical contact or that would interfere with duty equipment.

