## Enforcement

Uniform standards are enforced by supervisors at the station level.

<Steps>
  <Step title="First correction">
    Verbal correction from a supervisor. The deputy corrects the issue before resuming patrol.
  </Step>
  <Step title="Repeated issues">
    Documented and addressed by the deputy's chain of command.
  </Step>
  <Step title="Persistent non-compliance">
    Treated as a conduct issue, up to removal from patrol privileges.
  </Step>
</Steps>

Most uniform issues are unintentional and resolved in seconds. The standard exists so that every deputy on scene is immediately identifiable as SBCSD — to the public, to other units, and to allied agencies.
